feat core: make http clients wait for dynamic configs to be loaded

Several changes are made in order to ensure that http clients starts with actual settings from dynamic configs:

1. New synchronization primitive, @ref engine::MultiConsumerEvent, is added.
   It behaves similar to @ref engine::SingleUseEvent, but allows multiple consumers.
2. @ref components::DynamicConfig::NoblockSubscriber interface is updated - its old methods `GetEventSource` and `GetDiffSource` are replaced with single method `UpdateIfHasConfigAndListen`.
   New method executes callback not only for new dynamic configs updates, but also for current configs value if it was already set.
   It is a breaking change if you used @ref components::DynamicConfig::NoblockSubscriber - in that case you should update your code the following way:

   ```cpp
   class MyComponent {
   public:
     static constexpr std::string_view kName = "my-component-name";

     MyComponent(const components::ComponentConfig& config, const components::ComponentContext& context);

     ...
     // before, in case GetEventSource was used
     //
     // void OnConfigUpdate(const dynamic_config::Snapshot& snapshot);
     //
     // after
     void OnConfigUpdate(const dynamic_config::Diff& diff);
     // if GetDiffSource was used, OnConfigUpdate does not need to be changed
   private:
     ...
     concurrent::AsyncEventSubscriberScope subscriber_scope_;
   }

   MyComponent::MyComponent(const components::ComponentConfig& config, const components::ComponentContext& context) {
     ...
     subscriber_scope_ = components::DynamicConfig::NoblockSubscriber{config_component}
     // before
     //  .GetEventSource() or .GetDiffSource()
     //  .AddListener(this, kName, &MyComponent::OnConfigUpdate);
     // after
       .UpdateIfHasConfigAndListen(this, kName, &MyComponent::OnConfigUpdate);
   }

   // before, if GetEventSource was used
   // void MyComponent::OnConfigUpdate(const dynamic_config::Snapshot& snapshot) {
   //   DoUpdate(snapshot);
   // }
   // after
   void MyComponent::OnConfigUpdate(const dynamic_config::Diff& diff) {
     DoUpdate(diff.current);
   }
   ```
3. @ref components::HttpClientCore now has method `WaitUntilConfigSet` that suspends execution until dynamic configs are loaded or components loading is cancelled.
4. @ref components::HttpClient now has new configuration parameter, `wait-for-dynamic-configs`.
   If `wait-for-dynamic-configs` is explicitly set to true, @ref components::HttpClient calls @ref components::HttpClientCore::WaitUntilConfigSet before @ref clients::http::Client initialization.
   If `wait-for-dynamic-configs` is explicitly set to false, @ref components::HttpClientCore::WaitUntilConfigSet is not called.
   If `wait-for-dynamic-configs` is not set explicitly, it defaults to false for `dynamic-config-http-client` and to true for other clients.
   In case you use dynamic configs and don't want for http clients to wait for configs to be loaded, you should explicitly disable `wait-for-dynamic-configs` in `http-client` and other @ref components::HttpClient instances you use.
   If you don't use dynamic configs (`dynamic-config.updates-enabled` is set to false), there's no need to change `wait-for-dynamic-configs` - @ref components::HttpClientCore::WaitUntilConfigSet will return immediately
