feat engine: add utils::AsyncHideSpan

@ref utils::AsyncHideSpan is now the recommended way to span tasks without writing unwanted spans and consuming tracing quota. Logs will be attached to the nearest span that is written out. @ref engine::AsyncNoSpan should only be used to either intentionally detach the task from the trace, or as an optimization if there are no logs written inside. Read docs of @ref utils::AsyncHideSpan and @ref engine::AsyncNoSpan for more information.
